WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.901
-Donald Trump stormed out
of Manhattan courtroom

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.467
after he was called
to the witness stand

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.367
and reprimanded by a judge
for violating a gag order.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.934
And yet, Trump's legal woes
have not tempered

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.701
the Republican Party's
ongoing devotion to him,

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:15.601
as evidenced by their latest
choice for speaker Mike Johnson,

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.901
a right-wing hardliner
who helped engineer

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:20.634
Trump's attempts to overturn
the 2020 election.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.400
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.868
♪♪

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.367
We are all used
to the screaming,

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.033
blustery Trump
we see at rallies,

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.601
constantly ranting about
everything from

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.467
windmills killing birds
and whales

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.868
to toilets that don't flush

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.701
to various celebrities
who either are or are not

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.033
nasty to him.

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:42.234
That Trump is everywhere,
and it gets dumber every day,

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.534
like on Monday at a rally
in New Hampshire

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.801
when he claimed to have
had an epiphany.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.567
-I'm for us.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.100
I'm for us.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.067
You know how you
spell "us," right?

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.100
You spell "us" U-S.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.267
I just picked that up.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.801
Has anyone ever thought
of that before?

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:02.801
I just picked that up
a couple of days --

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:06.300
I'm reading and it said "us,"
and I said, you know,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.100
if you think about it,
"us" equals U-S.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.033
-Okay, so the bad news is,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:16.601
the Republican frontrunner for
the 2024 presidential nomination

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:21.000
is out here
designing pillows for TJ Maxx.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.234
The dude is dumb as dumb rocks.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.634
But the good news is
he would crush

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.901
a two-letter word spelling bee.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.200
"Your word is 'me.'"

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.901
"Can you use it
in a sentence, please?"

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:36.033
"You have got to be
[bleep] kidding me."

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:37.934
If I had come home from school

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.868
as a seven-year-old
and told my parents,

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:43.000
"Did you know 'us'
is spelled U and S?"

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.033
my parents would have
immediately called the school

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.300
and said, "I think we need
to make the curriculum

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.267
a little more challenging."

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.300
Well, my dad would have.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.634
My mom would have
called me a genius

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.167
and baked me a cake.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:57.567
But here's here's what's least
believable about that clip.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.701
-A couple of days,
I'm reading and it said "us."

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:03.234
-No, you weren't reading.
You don't read.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:04.634
You know how I know
you don't read?

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:08.667
If you did, you wouldn't have
discovered at age 77

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:13.267
that "us" is spelled
with a U and an S.

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.701
I mean, what have
you have been reading anyway

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.400
that would have spurred
such an epiphany?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.767
"Chicka Chicka Boom Boom"?

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.534
"A told B and B told C,

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.133
I'll meet you at the top
of the coconut tree.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:26.801
But it's too late.
I already chopped down the tree.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.567
And I replaced it with
a Trump resort!

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:29.634
There won't be any trees,

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:31.767
but there will be
plenty of coconuts,

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:35.100
if you know what I mean.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.033
That kid's shaking his head no.
He doesn't know what I mean."

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:43.267
-So that's the blustery,
unhinged, public Trump.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.901
But then there's the Trump
you don't get to see,

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:49.300
and that's the Trump who only
exists when he's under oath.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.801
And when he's under oath,
he's under penalty of perjury.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.634
He's suddenly much calmer.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:56.601
He's more restrained.
You could even say sheepish.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.968
Here he is, for example,
in a deposition from 2016

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:03.067
related to a restaurant that
pulled out of his D.C. hotel.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.467
-Good morning, Mr. Trump.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:05.701
And again, thank you very much
for being here.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.767
-Thank you.

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.634
-Would you state your full name
for the record, please?

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:11.200
-Donald John Trump.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.167
-And I imagine you've had
your deposition taken

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.000
a number of times?
-I have, yes.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.200
-So you know the drill.
-I do.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.067
-I won't waste anyone's time
going through it.

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.267
-Good. Thank you.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:20.667
-Do know that
if you need to take a break,

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.133
I'm happy to let you.
-Very good.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.434
Thank you.

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.968
-My understanding is that
you signed this lease.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.701
And if you look at page --
-That's true.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.234
He asked me, yeah.
-Okay.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:34.601
-Well, I did --
I believe I signed the lease,

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.968
but he came in and said,
"We're signing the lease."

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:39.100
I'll change it, yes.
-He said, "We're signing it"?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.934
-Because I think I signed it.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.267
Yeah. That's my signature. Yes.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.300
-"Yes, that's -- that's my name.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.200
And in fact,
I'm just picking this up now --

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.801
D and O together spells do.'

00:03:57.033 --> 00:04:00.934
So really, my name
should be Do-nald.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.634
If you think --
If you think about that."

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.968
That footage is amazing.

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:06.400
It's like watching
the neighborhood Rottweiler

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:07.901
who's always
terrorizing the mailman

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:09.801
suddenly mope around in a cone.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:12.701
Like, in public
he's a raving lunatic,

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.934
screaming [bleep] like,
"Radical woke Democrats

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.400
are using windmills and secret
satellites to kill Christmas."

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.901
And then, under oath,
he's practically Emily Post.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.334
"Thank you.
No, thank you very much.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:24.200
I would love to read
some incriminating documents.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.634
Thank you."

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:28.934
Because that's the only place
Trump faces consequences.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.634
That's the one way
you can still punish Trump,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.200
make him sit down
in a courtroom

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.801
and answer questions under oath
with his tail between his legs.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:36.367
And that's what happened
yesterday, when the judge

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.033
in his civil fraud trial hauled
him up to the witness stand

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.934
to reprimand him
for violating a gag order

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:42.734
that bars Trump
from attacking court staff.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.634
-Donald Trump,
taking the stand today

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.467
in his civil fraud trial
in New York

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:50.100
after being ordered by the judge
to testify about comments

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.567
he made regarding a court clerk.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:54.901
Trump claimed that
he wasn't talking about

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:56.501
the person
sitting next to the judge.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:59.067
He was actually talking
about Michael Cohen,

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.601
who at the time,
was in the middle of

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:02.601
his second day of testimony,

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.467
not the clerk.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:07.334
Judge Engoron was not buying it,
not for a nanosecond,

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.901
and he swiftly fined
Donald Trump $10,000

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.501
and rebuked Trump.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.667
-So Trump was ordered to take
the stand and explain himself,

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.000
and then the judge said,
"I don't believe you,"

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.133
and reprimanded him.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.400
I can only imagine
what that looked like.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.200
He was probably like
a middle schooler

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.701
who refuses to look
his parent in the eye

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:21.801
after cursing them out.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:22.801
"What did you just say?"

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:23.834
"Nothing."

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.367
"Tell me what you said."

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.400
"I said F you."

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.968
"Look at me when you say it."

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.033
"I said F you, okay?
It's not a curse word.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:33.167
I was talking about my favorite
band, the Foo Fighters.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:36.601
I was reading
and I just picked that up."

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:40.067
In fact, we don't have video or
photos of this historic moment,

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:43.067
but we do have a courtroom
sketch, and it's amazing.

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.434
Even in a courtroom sketch,
Trump is making a face like

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:47.701
he just realized
he's in trouble --

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:51.300
mouth slightly open, looking
at the judge like, "Uhhh."

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.434
Also, whoever drew this did
Trump some huge favors,

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.367
because this looks like
a "New Yorker" cartoon,

00:05:56.367 --> 00:06:00.334
where in reality
he's much more of a "Cathy."

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.734
And then,
like a pissy teenager,

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.167
Trump made things
even more dramatic

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.334
by storming out of the courtroom
less than an hour later.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:08.100
-This was a dramatic
turn of events, Lester.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.934
Former President Trump stormed
out of a Manhattan courtroom

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:12.634
after a tense day
after the judge

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:15.467
refused his attorney's request
to dismiss the case.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:17.567
-Michael Cohen
did resume testifying,

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:19.901
but Trump didn't stick around
to hear him finish,

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:24.133
the disgraced ex-president,
storming out of the courtroom

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:26.801
with Secret Service agents
left to chase after him.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:30.667
-Okay, "chase"
seems like a strong word.

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.200
They chased him the way
you chased your pet turtle

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.834
in the yard.

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:38.734
"He's going that way."

00:06:38.734 --> 00:06:42.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.234
I'm sure Secret Service
didn't have to run too hard.

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:46.667
They probably saw him take off
and said, "He's on the move.

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:51.467
Should we finish this game of
Monopoly and then go catch up?"

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:52.667
"But we haven't even started."

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.267
"We'll be fine."

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:56.634
We're talking about a guy
who moves slower than a zombie

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:59.567
after a giant bong rip.

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:02.767
-"You know what's a funny word?

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:05.834
Brains."

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:07.734
And then, just to give you
an idea of how defeated

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.234
Trump was after all that,
when he left the courtroom,

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:12.901
he gave the press a one-sentence
answer then walked away.

00:07:22.467 --> 00:07:24.267
-That wasn't even
one of his good lies.

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:28.167
The witness, Michael Cohen,
admitted Trump won the trial?

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:29.601
You know
there are transcripts right?

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:33.234
That lady isn't writing
in her diary.

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:35.400
Trump having to take the stand
and actually talk to the judge

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.634
clearly spun him out.

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:37.934
-"The witness said we won,

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:40.367
and the judge agreed and
apologized for the whole deal.

00:07:40.367 --> 00:07:44.434
And I'm so [bleep], you guys.
I'm so [bleep].

00:07:44.434 --> 00:07:48.701
They made me
sit next to the judge.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:51.667
That can't be good, right?"

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:54.734
And yet, the Republican Party
nonetheless remains in thrall

00:07:54.734 --> 00:07:56.567
to a man who just got scolded
by a judge

00:07:56.567 --> 00:07:57.934
in a courtroom
during a fraud trial,

00:07:57.934 --> 00:08:00.734
as evidenced by the fact
that they just elected a guy

00:08:00.734 --> 00:08:03.234
named Mike Johnson from
Louisiana as their new speaker.

00:08:03.234 --> 00:08:05.100
Johnson isn't just
an election denier.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.467
He was, according
to the "New York Times,"

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.667
"the most important architect
of the Electoral College

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:10.133
objections on January 6th."

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:13.968
And he's not just a guy who
thinks there was election fraud,

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:15.334
which would be wrong on its own,

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:18.167
he parroted the most bat[bleep]
crazy conspiracy theories

00:08:18.167 --> 00:08:19.334
you can imagine.

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:21.300
Remember Trump's ex-lawyer
Sidney Powell,

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.801
who just flipped
on him in Georgia?

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.701
Remember how she didn't just say
the usual GOP stuff

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:28.734
like "mail voting isn't secure,"
but went way off the deep end

00:08:28.734 --> 00:08:31.167
and claimed the Dominion
voting software was rigged

00:08:31.167 --> 00:08:34.033
by the dead Venezuelan President
Hugo Chavez?

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.400
-The Dominion Voting systems,

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.901
the Smartmatic
technology software,

00:08:39.901 --> 00:08:42.734
and the software that goes
in other computerized

00:08:42.734 --> 00:08:45.968
voting systems here as well,
not just Dominion,

00:08:45.968 --> 00:08:52.234
were created in Venezuela
at the direction of Hugo Chavez

00:08:52.234 --> 00:08:54.934
to make sure
he never lost an election.

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.934
-Now, we have played this clip
a few times lately,

00:08:56.934 --> 00:08:58.734
because Powell just pleaded
guilty in Georgia,

00:08:58.734 --> 00:09:01.000
and every time, it's impossible
not to be distracted

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.934
by Rudy Giuliani behind her,
sweating profusely

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:08.267
and trying to unscrew the cap
from a tiny water bottle

00:09:08.267 --> 00:09:11.634
like it has the antidote inside.

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:15.234
I think he's sweating because
he can't open the water bottle,

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:16.901
like it's slowly dawning
on him that

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:19.434
if he can't get
the cap off a Fiji bottle,

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.400
he might not be a good lawyer.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.534
"Oh boy, this is a bad sign.

00:09:24.534 --> 00:09:26.100
But when it's my turn
at the mic,

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:31.267
I'm going to blow them away or
my name's not Ruby Gugliotta."

00:09:31.267 --> 00:09:33.634
Anyway, that was the insane
conspiracy theory that,

00:09:33.634 --> 00:09:37.100
among other things, Fox News had
to pay nearly $800 million for

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:38.634
in a defamation suit.

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:41.234
And yet Mike Johnson,
the new Speaker of the House,

00:09:41.234 --> 00:09:43.567
actually thought
those claims had merit,

00:09:43.567 --> 00:09:45.801
as he said in a radio interview
at the time.

00:10:15.767 --> 00:10:17.634
-"And I'll tell you another
thing, I agree with Rudy.

00:10:17.634 --> 00:10:20.868
Those water bottles
are hard to open."

00:10:20.868 --> 00:10:23.300
That's how nuts this guy is.
He's just as crazy as Trump.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.434
It's just a style difference.

00:10:24.434 --> 00:10:27.801
Trump is Jigsaw
and Johnson is Dexter.

00:10:27.801 --> 00:10:29.133
He agreed with the lunatic

00:10:29.133 --> 00:10:30.834
who just pleaded guilty
to crimes in Georgia

00:10:30.834 --> 00:10:32.901
and repeated talking points
that caused Fox News

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:35.634
to pay out $800 million
to settle a defamation case.

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.467
He just says stuff in a normal,
mild-mannered, moderate voice

00:10:39.467 --> 00:10:41.868
the Republicans think will
make him easier to stomach.

00:10:41.868 --> 00:10:43.701
He's the kind of guy
who would curse you out,

00:10:43.701 --> 00:10:45.467
but instead of saying
the words "you [bleep],"

00:10:45.467 --> 00:10:46.534
he'd say --

00:10:46.534 --> 00:10:48.133
-U-S.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.667
-Didn't see it coming.

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:55.767
Didn't see it coming.

00:10:55.767 --> 00:10:57.467
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:57.467 --> 00:11:01.133
♪♪

